---
description: A PR does not go out with work it names as not done, or a figure it cannot explain
alwaysApply: true
---

# No open ends in a PR

A PR is opened when its work is finished, not when it runs. These sentences do not belong in a PR body or in a report to the owner:

- "Not measured." A PR that adds a step on a measured path (license verification, server startup, checkout and renewal, binary size) measures it before it is opened, tunes what stands out, and reports the numbers before and after under the PR's `## Measurements`. What is left is stated with a number and the reason it stays.
- "We take it that ..., not checked." An explanation that one look can check is checked before it is written.
- "The cause is not confirmed." A figure or a failure the agent cannot explain is traced to its cause from the data before the PR is opened. A guess is not written as an explanation, with or without "probably".

What is out of the row's scope is a roadmap row that names when (`.cursor/rules/defer.mdc`), not a caveat. A finding about code the row did not change becomes its own Issue at once (`.cursor/rules/pace.mdc`).

A reason written as likely ("probably", 「と考えられる」) is checked first when a cheap check exists.

- A figure that moves after a change is traced by measuring again with that one change switched off. In M4a1 an audited write fell from 3.1–3.5 ms to 1.1 ms after the data layer moved to a query builder; with SQLite's WAL mode switched off the same build took 3.7–5.0 ms, so the cause was WAL, not the builder (PR #47).
- A measurement that needs what the local machine lacks (a PostgreSQL server, another OS) is taken on CI, in a step that prints the value to the job summary. In M4a1 the first PR body said the start time on PostgreSQL was not measured, and the review asked for it (PR #47).
- A value from a GitHub-hosted runner is written as the range of more than one run, with the reason: each run gets another machine. In M4a1 two runs of the same step gave 437–463 ms and 270–291 ms (PR #47).
- A value compared with an earlier build names that build (its commit). In M4a2 two sizes of the M4a1 build stood in the design, 2,048 bytes apart, and neither said which build it was (PR #55).

A figure of a step taken off a measured path stays in the design as the result before and after (16 ms → 7 ms). Its breakdown may stay in the PR body, as measured facts; a cause that was not found is not written in either. If the cause matters, it becomes a roadmap row. In M4b2 the design said the cause of 8 ms was "not known", and two reviews in a row asked for it to go (PR #67).

A comment in the code is held to the same line: it says what was measured, and marks a cause that was not confirmed as not confirmed, with the Issue number.

```text
# BAD
トークン検証の速度は詰めていません。初回だけ遅いですが、おそらく JIT です。

# GOOD
トークン検証は NativeAOT で 1 件 41 µs → 18 µs。内訳を測ると公開鍵の ImportSubjectPublicKeyInfo が 6 割だったので、
鍵 ID ごとに ECDsa を作って使い回すようにした。初回の 2.1 ms は ECDsa の生成で、JIT ではない（JitInfo で確認）。
```
